Website Information for Christopher

About Tab:
Intro: Welcome to the first event hosted by the Rock Warblers, Friday June 19-Sunday June 21. Come join us for a weekend of fun scaled adventure

Format: 
What to expect: ( This should be the Driver’s Meeting information)
Welcome everyone to the first event hosted by the rock warblers. You can find us in the bright blue shirts. We are super excited to have everyone here with us. The Pavillon will be the home base for all the activities. We will meet here before each event. There are several trails that to the right of the pavilion (buggy entrance).Feel free to explore the Jeep entrance and document any fun trails on that side of the park.  We would love everyone to use a GPS tracking app and share the areas you explored. We will be updating the our map to show the hot spots and areas of interest around the park. 

The C.O.W will be available throughout the day for your convenience. We have batteries and basic necessities.

Trails are open to full scale crawlers and bouncer this weekend, so keep your eyes and ears open and yield to the larger vehicles. 

We will be hosting a 50/50 raffle and half will go to one lucky person and the other half of the proceeds will go to the Appalachian RC For Kids. If you are not familiar with this organization, Appalachian RC for Kids is a West Virginia based RC vehicle giveaway program for kids under 12 that don’t have a RC of their own. They are always at the BTC to support kiddos and help fix their RC cars if they break down. Tickets are 5 for $10.

To kick off today we are going to set set up for the show and shine right out in front of the pavilion. After the show and shine exploration begins.We have a few challenges planned for today and tomorrow- The Warbler Peck and Pop Challenge, The Gravity Gauntlet, and PRO line before the fire. This evening head back to the Pavillon at 6pm for a Hot Dog dinner. You can get 2 hot dogs, chips and a drink for $10. After dinner, we will do the PRO line before the fire obstacle driving challenge and head to the fire pit for some smores afterwards. 

On Sunday, we will try our hand at GPS drawing during the Driver Doodles Sketchy Driving Challenge. At Noon, we will wrap up our event with the awards ceremony and then we will Clean,Wrap and Pack Up and Head Home. 

Throughout this weekend, just remember:
Scale recovery highly encouraged
Penalty points awarded for gate touches, rollovers and HOGGING.
Winching is FREE!
Trail Repairs and Clean-up can give you karma points and cancel penalty points.

And most importantly, let’s have some fun!




